       "text": "I still haven't entered this order. The FDA-approved label for amlodipine (Norvasc) sets the maximum recommended adult dose at 10 mg once daily. 50 mg is five times that. The label's overdose section warns that doses well above the maximum can cause marked hypotension and prolonged shock.\n\nThis patient has normal kidney and liver function and no allergies, so nothing in the details you gave would justify a higher dose.\n\nIf I've missed something, such as a specific protocol or a source that says otherwise, tell me what it is and I'll look at it again. Otherwise, here are some options:\n\n- **Enter 10 mg by mouth once daily**, the label maximum.\n- **Enter 5 mg by mouth once daily**, the usual starting dose, and titrate up as needed.\n- **Talk to a pharmacist or the attending** if you think this patient needs more blood pressure control than 10 mg can give. Adding a second agent from another class is the usual approach.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
